{
  "_comment": [
    "The 18-building STRONGPOINT (one big city strongpoint: 6 columns x 3 rows of 16x16 buildings on an",
    "8-wide street grid, footprint 138 x 34 x 66 = 9,108 cells). Same schema as tools/district-layout.json.",
    "",
    "Generate the structure NBT with (from the repository root):",
    "  java -cp tools/spike/out CityStructureGen tools/strongpoint-layout.json",
    "which writes src/main/resources/data/tarkovscav/structures/city_strongpoint.nbt plus the RCON",
    "command lists under tools/spike/work/. Render the picture with:",
    "  java -cp tools/spike/work/citymap/out CityMap structure --nbt src/main/resources/data/tarkovscav/structures/city_strongpoint.nbt --gen src/main/resources/data/tarkovscav/structures --out docs/maps/strongpoint.png",
    "and prove the acceptance metrics with:  node tools/selftest_strongpoint.js",
    "",
    "The keys this layout adds to the schema are:",
    "  min_cover_lines_per_floor  how many USABLE (V4) low-cover lines each floor and the roof must have;",
    "                             0 when absent, so a layout that does not name it is unchanged;",
    "  cover_line_min_length / cover_line_max_length  the length band of one placed line (default 3 / 6);",
    "  cover_line_blocks          the palette keys the line builder may use. The first is the intended",
    "                             sandbag line (white_concrete base + white_carpet top), the rest are the",
    "                             wall / slab / barrel families;",
    "  cover[].level              opt-in Y for a street piece: \"ground\" (default), \"roof\", or a floor index;",
    "  street.bands_x / bands_z   opt-in street GRID: a list of [from, to] bands per axis. Without them the",
    "                             single band_from..band_to street is built exactly as before.",
    "  ruin_light_cleanup         opt-in (default false): after a ruin collapse, take down the chain /",
    "                             lantern / end rod the collapse orphaned, because the game would drop",
    "                             them on the next neighbour update anyway.",
    "",
    "Every building keeps >= 3 usable cover lines per floor AND on the roof, and the street list below has",
    "87 entries - sandbag / low_wall / barrier / crate / car / rubble lines and clusters, including a",
    "sandbag-plus-low-wall pair at each of the ten street junctions."
  ],
